@startbpmn BP08_SetADaysFocus
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP08_SetADaysFocus.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP08_SetADaysFocus.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - the day is the unit of focus, settable from any period scope: BR-40, BR-93
'   - any date is focusable, past or future, with no restriction: BR-40, SA 2026-10-10
'   - committing a focus replaces the date's previous selection: BR-41, SA 2026-10-10
'   - boards and routines are what a day selects: BR-41
'   - the selection shape is 0..N projects and 0..M activities inside each: BR-41, SA 2026-10-10
'   - picking a project offers its ready activities: BR-41, BR-99
'   - selecting a routine CREATES its task where none is outstanding, on Chores - never a second one
'     while one is open, which is what the step says rather than ensuring anything: BR-42,
'     SA 2026-10-18 (the same reading as BP17's template step)
'   - due and overdue are treated identically: BR-42, BR-91
'   - deselecting a routine never removes a task already created: BR-42
'   - only non-archived projects and active routines are selectable: BR-43
'   - a routine has no theme, so the routines are offered as one list: BR-02, SA 2026-10-13
'   - Chores joins the day derived, never selected, while it carries open work: BR-107
'   - NEITHER CHAIN carries Chores. The write does not put it in play, because nothing stores that
'     membership: the routine tasks the commit ensures are what Chores carries, and carrying them is
'     what puts it in play, derived wherever the day is reported. The read does not report it
'     either: nothing in this process can act on an unfinished chore, and composing a day is not
'     where that work is shown - the board strip derives it when the user comes to work (BP11):
'     BR-107, BR-118, POL-12, SA 2026-10-17
'   - the day focus is a record of a human commitment: BR-40
'   - the advisor may propose a day's focus; applying it runs this same operation: BR-72
'   - the editor opens on a date that may already carry a focus, so the surface read carries that
'     date's committed selection: a surface is read whole, and what is already picked is what the
'     user drops. F-6 of 08_BP-Review-Findings.md is closed with it: BR-41, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-16
'   - the write answers with the focus it committed, so there is nothing left to re-read: a
'     client that just wrote the state knows it, and a state change elsewhere reaches the client
'     as that change's own answer. Call site BP08.03 (Read the day's focus) is RETIRED, its id
'     never reused: SA 2026-10-16, ADR-066
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'   - the offer carries each activity-based project's activities, so what the readiness calculation
'     works on is named where it is taken rather than in a fetch of its own: BR-99, SA 2026-10-17
'
' Scope: this process sets the focus for one date. Choosing which period to look at is UIP02, which hands
' over here by opening the day focus editor on the day the user picked.
'
' Call-site collapsing: scheduling the day's routine tasks is not a chain of its own. Selection
' is what creates the task, so the creation is a drawn step inside the one write.

pool "User" {
  start "A day to commit to"
  :Pick or drop the projects to work on;
  multiInstance

  :Pick or drop the activities inside each activity-based project;
  multiInstance
  rule BR-41
  note "Zero to many per project. The ready ones are offered first; nothing forces one at a time. A simple project contributes its own board and has no activities to pick."

  :Pick or drop the routines to keep up;
  multiInstance
  :Commit the day's focus;
  send "Set the day's focus" to setIn
  receive "What was committed, or why not" as focusSet
  note "Chores is never picked. It joins the day on its own while it carries work that is not done."

  end "Day committed"
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Day focus submitted" as setIn
  call "BP08.02_SetTheDaysFocus" "Set the day's focus" {
    :Replace the date's selection with what was committed;
    rule BR-41
    :Create the task a selected routine owes, where none is outstanding, on Chores;
    rule BR-42
    rule BR-102
    :Report the outcome, with the day's focus;
  }
  send "What was committed, or why not" to focusSet
  note "A commit replaces the date's previous selection rather than adding to it, so the boards in play are exactly what was last committed. A routine that already owes a task gets no second one, on any date. Due and overdue are treated the same. Dropping a routine leaves a task already created where it is."
  end "Day focus answered"
}

@endbpmn
